## Hot tier expansion (#320)

AVX-2 align(32) and AVX-512 align(64) Hot tiers are deferred to #320
with bench-driven evidence per the audit's H1 finding. Current Hot
ships with align(16) baseline only via AlignedWideBits16. If bench
evidence justifies the storage overhead, opt-in `HotAvx2` / `HotAvx512`
strategy variants ship as consumer-visible markers (toolbox-not-policer
compliant). The cfg-driven internal alignment originally proposed in
#316's first topic was rejected.

## Asm microkernels (#321)

Hot-path bit ops on WideBits / AlignedWideBits16 (count_ones,
trailing/leading_zeros, bitwise) get asm-microkernel implementations
when bench evidence shows compiler-generated SIMD doesn't hit the
inlined-instruction-count target. Drops down a tier from
intrinsic-load to inline asm only with measured justification.

## HotTruncate research (#322)

A possible future Hot variant that explicitly truncates wide widths
to 128 for compute (lossy but native-fast). Deferred for research.
Not in the current strategy lattice.

